details:
Here are some bugs that i've encountered with the IK system:
- IK breaks while crouching (the feet slide when the animator detects a crouched down position, regression from 2.0, happens on pretty much every 3.0 that I've tested). This was introduced with the 3.0 update;
- IK stops working for a few seconds after stopping movement (noticed this with every avatar 3.0 and 2.0). This was introduced recently after the 3.0 update;
(All this tested with a Valve Index + Controllers, no FBT)

To reproduce;  

Make a non-humanoid bone on your avatar (ie;  Not one that's Rigged.  A hair, or something).  Put a Contact Receiver in an empty transform.  It can be a child of the bone, or elsewhere, but must target the bone as its root transform.

Change the scaling of it in-game, along with the scaling of your avatar.  The position will now be offset.
